          <p>
            Our rule of thumb is simple. If most of your work is on cars and crossovers, buy mid-torque. If you regularly work on three-quarter-ton trucks, equipment or anything badly rusted, buy high-torque. If you already own a 1/2-inch wrench, add a compact 3/8-inch as your second tool rather than stepping up to a bigger one.
          </p>
